# =============================================================================
# lab/splunk/.gitignore - keep the Splunk second-SIEM stack's generated and
# tenant-derived files out of git.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STAND-IN context: Splunk Enterprise 60-day TRIAL in a local container
# (replaces production Splunk); see README.md.
#
# WHY A LOCAL .gitignore: splunk-up.sh writes .env (admin password + HEC token)
# on its very first run. This file makes that safe on its own, without
# depending on the repo-root .gitignore being updated first. Paths here are
# relative to lab/splunk/. (The root .gitignore may list the same paths; the
# duplication is harmless.)
# =============================================================================

# Generated admin password + HEC token (mode 0600). Never commit.
/.env

# Replay high-water marks, the verified-app fingerprint and --dry-run
# payloads (the payloads are real tenant sign-in data).
/.state/

# Edits made in Splunk Web land in the bind-mounted app's local/ and
# metadata/local.meta - they silently diverge from detections/*.spl, so they
# are never committed. Change the .spl file and re-render instead.
/app/contoso_identity/local/
/app/contoso_identity/metadata/local.meta

# Tenant-sensitive lookups: the operator's own IP (dc-logon detection) and the
# SoD holdings snapshot (object ids + UPNs, from 09-SoD-Report.ps1
# -HoldingsSnapshotPath). splunk-up.sh creates header-only copies when they
# are missing; the filled files never reach git.
/app/contoso_identity/lookups/contoso_operator_ips.csv
/app/contoso_identity/lookups/contoso_sod_holdings.csv
